.TH URSINECTL 1 "November 2026" "Ursine 0.25.4" "Ursine Manual"
.SH NAME
ursinectl \- Ursine root control CLI (in-process, chroot-capable)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ursinectl
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-as\-user
.IR USER ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.I module
.I action
.RI [ key=value ...]
.PP
.B ursinectl
.B \-\-help
.RI [ module ]
.br
.B ursinectl
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ursinectl
is the Ursine command-line interface for system administration. It hosts
the same core as the
.BR ursined (1)
daemon in-process: no daemon, no socket and no service manager are
required, so it also works inside a FeralOS chroot during installation.
.PP
Every invocation is root-only: the effective uid is checked before any
side effect and there is no override. Invoke it through
.B sudo
or from a root shell. Every action is written to the shared audit log
.RB ( /var/log/ursine/audit.jsonl )
with principal
.IR root .
.PP
This manual documents the complete command surface; keep it in parity
with the CLI (any new action, option or exit-code change updates this
page in the same change set).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result as one compact JSON line (for scripts). Without it the
result is pretty-printed JSON.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Confirm a destructive action. Without it the CLI refuses the action and
exits with status 2.
.TP
.BI \-\-as\-user " USER"
Target another account for the user-scoped modules
.RB ( packages_nix ,
theming, crontab). The account must exist and be a normal login user;
unknown accounts fail with a typed
.I user <name> does not exist
before any capability gate. Root may target any existing login account;
non-root principals (the GUI) only their own.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Configuration file; default
.IR /etc/ursine/config.toml .
Must be a regular file and not group/world-writable.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage, or the action list of a single module
.RB ( ursinectl \-\-help
.IR nix ).
Does not require root.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit. Does not require root.
.SH VALUE SYNTAX
Arguments are
.IR key=value
pairs.
.TP
\(bu
Values are parsed as JSON when possible
.RB ( dry_run=true ,
.BR keep=3 ,
.BR value={"...":...} ),
otherwise they are plain strings.
.TP
\(bu
.BI key= @path
reads the value from a file;
.BI key= \-
reads it from stdin.
.TP
\(bu
Unknown keys are rejected (exit 2); a typo never runs silently.
.TP
\(bu
Secrets (
.I password
,
.I new_password
) must be passed as
.BR key= \-
(stdin). Values on the command line are refused (argv is visible in
.IR /proc ).
.SH COMMANDS
Action names are the stable wire names (same as the API tag and the audit
log). Run
.B ursinectl \-\-help
for the grouped list.
.TP
.B system
.BR status ,
.BR job_output .
.TP
.B config
.BR init ,
.BR get_config ,
.BR set_module_switch .
.TP
.B capabilities
.BR list ,
.BR refresh .
.TP
.B packages_nix
list_installed, search, install, remove, remove_all, remove_regex,
upgrade, upgrade_regex, generations, rollback, wipe_history,
diff_closures, store_gc, prune_generations.
.TP
.B packages_apk
list_apk, search_apk, refresh_apk, list_apk_repositories, install_apk,
preview_apk_install, remove_apk, upgrade_apk, list_apk_updates,
upgrade_apk_package.
.TP
.B packages_flatpak
list_flatpak, list_flatpak_remotes, search_flatpak, install_flatpak,
get_flatpak_info, remove_flatpak, update_flatpak, update_flatpak_app,
remove_flatpak_orphans.
install_flatpak accepts an optional remote (default flathub);
get_flatpak_info reports name, version, download and installed size for
the install confirmation.
.TP
.B printers
list_printers, printer_jobs, add_printer, add_printer_manual,
remove_printer, set_default_printer, set_printer_options, pause_printer,
cancel_printer_jobs.
.TP
.B scanners
list_scanners, get_scanner_config, set_scanner_device,
remove_scanner_device, set_scanner_discovery.
.TP
.B network
get_network, set_wifi_enabled, connect_wifi, connect_network,
disconnect_network.
.TP
.B bluetooth
get_bluetooth, set_bluetooth_power, scan_bluetooth, bluetooth_action.
.TP
.B disks
list_disks, mount_disk, unmount_disk.
.TP
.B services
list_services, service_action.
.TP
.B firewall
get_firewall, set_default_firewall_zone, add_firewall_service,
remove_firewall_service, add_firewall_port, remove_firewall_port,
reload_firewall.
.TP
.B snapshots
list_snapshots, stats, create_snapshot, restore_snapshot,
get_btrbk_config, init_btrbk_config, set_btrbk_config, delete_snapshot,
delete_snapshots.
.TP
.B users
list_users, create_user, delete_user, set_password, list_groups,
set_groups.
.TP
.B niri
get_niri_config, validate_niri_config, set_niri_section.
get_niri_config reports version, version_parsed, version_supported and
min_supported. validate_niri_config returns valid, the raw niri output,
and field-level errors (message, line, column, section, field); a false
valid exits with status 1 even though the call succeeded.
.TP
.B theming
theme_detect, theme_get, theme_apply.
.TP
.B logs
log_list, log_read, log_search (paths relative to
.IR /var/log ;
escapes and binary files are rejected).
.TP
.B crontab
crontab_get, crontab_set. Operations run as root through the portable
.B crontab \-u <user>
form: no
.B su
impersonation and no suid bit on the tool.
.SH DESTRUCTIVE ACTIONS
Removing, deleting, rolling back, garbage collecting and applying
restores/crontab/theme changes require
.B \-\-yes
(the CLI equivalent of the GUI confirmation). Dry-run and preview
variants never do. Without the flag the CLI prints the refused action and
exits with status 2.
.SH BACKGROUND JOBS
Package mutations answer with a job id; the CLI streams the job log to
stdout as plain terminal text (never a percentage bar) and exits with the
job's exit code. CLI job logs live under
.IR /run/ursine/cli-jobs .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including a background mutation that exited 0).
.TP
.B 1
Action/API error: capability gate, validation, job failure. The message
goes to stderr with a
.B fix:
hint when available.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: bad arguments, unknown module/action/field, missing
.BR \-\-yes ,
or the root gate.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ursine/config.toml
Module switches and daemon paths (shared with ursined).
.TP
.I /var/log/ursine/audit.jsonl
Append-only audit log; every CLI action is recorded.
.TP
.I /run/ursine/cli-jobs/
Background-job logs of the CLI (tmpfs, per-process subdirectories).
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/ursinectl
Installed binary (install.sh, or the nix profile via ursine-activate).
.SH NOTES
Inside a chroot all absolute paths resolve against the chroot root, so
.B ursinectl caps list
works as a health probe of the target system with no services running.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ursined (1),
the guide
